{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787089244809987001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"dietetic-pompous-boar","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"a4670648615f72e0e7227c34201ec52ea7063575315740dc9ea2af4ae9127292","event_uuid":"5d0c94b9-3c08-49d5-9c23-830410f69bd4","position":{"commit_sha":"19ac569675b06d42df549ea8315e670283f332f7","position":"1787080906460373001-5d0c94b9-3c08-49d5-9c23-830410f69bd4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0d70ba4afd6420fbc07182c8552b450bb06d08ce989a760eebf78458ef88dbc2","event_uuid":"bbfe61aa-51a7-43ea-a572-2ffbbe66cf04","position":{"commit_sha":"aa3f152e67e29e8e6a61001868430ab00c596bd8","position":"1787080925365171001-bbfe61aa-51a7-43ea-a572-2ffbbe66cf04"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"71857de880318a1a63e875c5d0bea1a2c316070bf0872336fecbf659ab7c2833","event_uuid":"6d71ef19-81cb-485d-bd82-ffef18793520","position":{"commit_sha":"e1c91b8cd9a81f6215792ca3c917017bd956c542","position":"1787083233193223001-6d71ef19-81cb-485d-bd82-ffef18793520"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787080906460373001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6d71ef19-81cb-485d-bd82-ffef18793520","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ba48-a88a-92bd-45d0"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe review gates currently read effective criteria and routing through multiple seams. Code review then consults packaged-only overlay and detector registries, so a project disable or retune can be ignored and an activated project DET criterion can disappear. Separate reads can also describe different repository policy states. RP-06 requires one immutable authority before any selection or model call.\n\n## Approach\nCreate a repository-bound `CriteriaSnapshot` in `rebar.llm.criteria`. It compiles effective built-ins, project LLM criteria, project DET criteria, prompt/routing/posture/applicability metadata, source locations, and one deterministic digest from the provided repository root and already-resolved operation inputs. Consumers receive the snapshot; they do not reread ambient policy.\n\nKeep applicability vocabularies gate-specific. For project code-review LLM criteria, validate `applies_to` as a non-empty list of non-empty repository-relative globs and define `[\"**\"]` as repository-wide. No changed path match produces a typed non-applicable selection reason. Built-in secondary triggers remain unchanged, project DET selection remains detector-owned, and plan review retains `applies_at` and `trigger`. Migrate `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` entry `project.review-phase-boundaries` from `[]` to `[\"**\"]` so its current all-review behavior is explicit.\n\nRecord an ADR describing snapshot ownership, gate-specific applicability, the explicit global-glob spelling, and why a single effective authority is preferable to gate-specific registry reads. The snapshot is data and policy only; it does not interpret YAML/BPMN topology, execute criteria, or decide verdicts.\n\n## Migration and Rollback\nAdd the snapshot alongside existing registry readers. Golden contract tests compare the snapshot-derived selection inputs with current behavior when no project overlay is present and allow only the approved corrections for effective disables/retunes, project DET inclusion, and project LLM applicability. Existing registry APIs remain as compatibility adapters until the dependent cutover stories land; rollback is a code revert, not a new configuration flag.\n\n## Testing\nUse in-process unit and real producer-to-consumer contract tests. One tier lower is insufficient because the known defects occur between the overlay producer and packaged-routing consumers. Tests feed real project routing files through the loader and snapshot compiler, then assert exact selected policy, source provenance, and digest behavior. Negative controls cover built-in empty secondary triggers and plan-review routing, which must not adopt the new project-LLM glob rule.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A real project overlay compiled through `CriteriaSnapshot` yields one immutable digest-bound view containing effective built-in, project LLM, and project DET policy with source provenance.\n- [ ] A project code-review LLM criterion with an empty, missing, non-list, or blank `applies_to` fails before any model call with its criterion id, configuration location, and the remedy `use [\"**\"] for repository-wide`.\n- [ ] Given root, nested, and dot paths, `applies_to: [\"**\"]` selects the criterion exactly once; a nonmatching scoped glob records non-applicable selection without executing it.\n- [ ] `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` declares `project.review-phase-boundaries.applies_to` as `[\"**\"]`, and a contract test proves its review membership is unchanged by the migration.\n- [ ] Contract tests prove effective built-in disables/retunes and activated project DET entries are present in the snapshot while built-in secondary-trigger and plan-review routing semantics remain unchanged.\n- [ ] An ADR documents snapshot ownership, digest inputs, gate-specific applicability, compatibility adapters, and the revert-based rollback.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/criteria/snapshot.py","reason":"New immutable effective-policy snapshot and digest types."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/criteria/overlay.py","reason":"Validate project code-review LLM applicability and compile source-located policy."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/criteria/__init__.py","reason":"Expose the snapshot seam to review gates."},{"path":".rebar/criteria_routing.json","reason":"Migrate project.review-phase-boundaries to the explicit repository-wide glob."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_criteria_snapshot.py","reason":"Producer-to-consumer snapshot, digest, applicability, and negative-control contracts."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_criteria_overlay.py","reason":"Located invalid-project-glob validation coverage."},{"path":"docs/adr/0099-review-discovery-effective-policy.md","reason":"Architecture decision for the unified review-policy snapshot."},{"path":"docs/adr/README.md","reason":"Index the new ADR."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","58bd-d656-c52f-4cf4"],["relates_to","ba48-a88a-92bd-45d0"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"58bd-d656-c52f-4cf4","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["rp-06","llm","criteria","architecture"],"ticket_id":"60c1-80de-a22f-4d39","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-06 S1 — Compile immutable effective review-policy snapshots","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5d0c94b9-3c08-49d5-9c23-830410f69bd4","bbfe61aa-51a7-43ea-a572-2ffbbe66cf04","6d71ef19-81cb-485d-bd82-ffef18793520"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787089244809987001,"uuid":"33cc3073-6556-4b7f-b3fc-0514ec476c38"}